# compiler/tests/native/targets-emit.sh: the programs and lIR cases that do not lower for a triple today, one "TRIPLE PATH" per line.
# A line is removed when its cause is fixed; the script fails when this list and what fails differ.
# These two lIR cases name an x86 CPU in their (target (cpu ..)) form: the RISC-V backend aborts ("LLVM ERROR: RV64 target requires an RV64 CPU");
# wasm and aarch64 only warn and ignore it. A module's CPU of another architecture should be a diagnostic of lairf, not an LLVM abort (targets.md 3.1).
riscv64-unknown-linux-gnu cases/lir/simd/target-cpu-only.lir
riscv64-unknown-linux-gnu cases/lir/simd/target.lir
